{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He will cut off</b> — by way of metaphor, like the meaning of <i>He will cut</i> [from] the root בצר. And this is connected, for all the regions around Jerusalem will bring tribute when they see, for HaShem cuts off the spirit of princes, that He is awesome to the kings of earth, as in: <i>over all the kings of the earth</i>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 76, :notes {0 "The comment interprets יבצור as from the root בצר 'to cut off,' apparently connecting it to an elided verse phrase; the referent of כי כל סביבות ירושלם יובילו שי בראותם is not fully spelled out in the source text."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:43.033080307Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}